Q60. What are Top 5 REST guidelines and the advantages of them ?
    Answer:
        REST GUIDELINES
        ---------------
            1. Separation of Client And Server
                The implementation of the client and the server must be done independently.
                Advantage: Independence allows easier maintenance, scalability and evolution.
            2. Stateless
                The server will not store anything about the latest HTTP request the client made.
                Advantage: It will treat every request as new request. It simlifies server implementation as it is not overloading it with state management.
            3. Uniform Interface
                Identify the resources by URL (eg. www.abc.com/api/question)
                Advantage: Standarized URLs, making it easy to understand and use the API.
            4. Cacheable
                The API response should be cacheable to improve the performance.
                Advantage: Caching API responses Improves performances by reducing the need of repeated requests to the server.
            5. Layered System
                The system sould follow layered pattern.
                Advantage: A layered system, such as the Model-View-Controller (MVC) pattern, promotes modular design and separation of concerns.

Q61. What are difference between REST API and SOAP API ?
    Answer:
        REST API:
            -> Architecture: REST is an architectural state.
            -> Potocol: Uses HTTP & HTTPS.
            -> Message Format: Uses light-weight formats like JSON, XML.
            -> State: Stateless
            -> Error Handling: Relies on HTTP status code.
            -> Performance: Generally lightweight and faster.

        SOAP API:
            -> Architecture: SOAP (Simple Object Access Protocol) is a protocol.
            -> Protocol: Can use various protocols (HTTP, SMTP etc.)
            -> Message format: Typically uses XML.
            -> State: Can be stateless and stateful.
            -> Error handling: Defines it own fault mechanism.
            -> Performace: Can be slower due to XML processing.

